e-decided 178(i)), STATUS and `next.json` to say so.\n- **The camera image now needs a queue.** The frame image path `#6810 → #5058 'Image In'` has been added to the queue stage (QRT) as a connection still to be built.\n- **Tools fixed along the way:**\n  - The launch check now accepts the simulator's own plan format; every L2 stage would otherwise have been blocked.\n  - The simulator now handles a loop-boundary connection the way LabVIEW actually does, confirmed against a real read of the file.\n  - `guard_peer` now lets a review clear a failed run only if that review covered the same script. Before, a review that merely mentioned the script was enough.\n- **Why it took 7 dispatches:** two early attempts were blocked by the launch check before the plan-format fix went in; the retrospective says building that fix first would have saved one dispatch and about $1.\n\n**Cycle 80's first act (`next.json`), before any L2-A1 work:**\n1. Read the wires on `#3173` and `#9519` in the K file. If they are on wire 23807, K stands. If they carry no wire, a small stage wires them. Any other wire means K is rejected and re-run from `D1_s4_loop17.vi`.\n2. Remove the whitelist, with a self-test, so a step error always stops the run.\n3. Build a reader that can see panel-indicator wiring.\n\n**Still owed:** 8 launch-gate self-test cases that have been failing since cycle 78, and a trim of STATUS.md (about 140 lines against the ~100 limit).\n\nNo new questions for you from this cycle. The one open item from cycle 77 (`D-2026-09-25-01`, your typical bead count and run length) is still waiting and blocks nothing. The Figma connector needs authorizing in your claude.ai connector settings if you want it; this cycle did not use it.","ttft_ms":2310,"type":"result","duration_ms":6651207,"uuid":"9156adac-17f1-414c-9d18-3e15656249dc","ttft_stream_ms":1932,"time_to_request_ms":211,"first_content_frame_ms":1932,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
